% Per-unit warning suppression: a rule that is both dead and wrong.
%
% `integer(X)` at a `color`-typed position is contradicting evidence,
% so the rule can never fire (YCHR-20104); `R = X` then writes a
% `color` into an `int`-typed argument, which is an inconsistency. A
% unit that reports an error omits its warnings, so only the error is
% reported — see docs/reference/type-system.md §Inaccessible branches.
:- module(typecheck_suppression_same_unit, []).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

:- chr_type color ---> red ; green ; blue.
:- chr_constraint tag(color, int).

dead @ tag(X, R) <=> integer(X) | R = X.
